    <string name="readiness_info" formatted="false">Readiness combines last night\'s measurements with your recent training, each compared with your own normal rather than with population averages.\n\n# What goes in\n- HRV, 35 %: the 7-day average of nightly HRV against your normal range from the last 60 days.\n- Sleep, 25 %: last night\'s sleep score and the average of the last three nights.\n- Resting heart rate, 20 %: last night against your usual.\n- Training, 20 %: form against a band that grows with your fitness.\n\n# Safeguards\n- While your HRV is below its normal range, readiness stays below \"Ready to train\", as HRV-guided training studies recommend.\n- A breathing rate clearly above usual, together with low HRV or a raised resting heart rate, holds readiness at 40 or below: a common early sign of illness.\n\n# How much to trust it\nThe HRV comparison has the strongest research behind it. The weights are PacingLab\'s own choice, not a validated score. Readiness needs 14 nights of HRV and settles after four to eight weeks.</string>

